=== Interpretation ===

H1 ("Cyclone IV LE reads only the 16 LUT data cells at runtime") is
implicitly validated for mask=0xFFFF at this pin-friendly position:
σ⁻¹-only XOR onto mask=0x0000 baseline produced a chip that, when cold-
booted, has the LE truth table = 0xFFFF at (X=22, Y=12, N=4) — with no
collateral edits anywhere else in the pin-friendly grid (single hit
from the scan).

H2 ("LE reads canon-cells or routing-CRAM at runtime") is **REFUTED**
for the symmetric-mask case: the codec didn't write any canon-cell or
routing-CRAM bits, yet the LE's truth table is correct.

H2 for ASYMMETRIC masks (e.g., 0x6996) remains gated until either the
Quartus Lite LCCOMB-lock toolchain blocker is resolved or a Path-D
alternative test is designed.  The symmetric-only first ship of mode H
is silicon-validated as of this capture.
